     "byScheme": true,
     "rule": "A recessed fill, a step below content.",
     "pick": "neutral.100, a step below content (1.17:1 on surface.default), so table headers and wells read as recessed.",
     "darkPick": "neutral.50: We use one step darker than content for table headers and wells in dark, in order to show depth by tone, 1.16:1 on surface.default. The darker fill does this by the depth rule turned downward: what sits lower is darker. So a well reads as recessed and never as a raised card, because dark ships as standard (theming.values) and depth reads from tone and lines (elevation.definition).",
